---
// Accessibility statement. States the target, what was built in, the known limits and the feedback route.
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site, formatDate } from '../data/site';

const toc = [
  { id: 'commitment', title: 'Our commitment' },
  { id: 'what-we-did', title: 'What we did' },
  { id: 'known-limits', title: 'Known limits' },
  { id: 'report', title: 'Report a barrier' },
  { id: 'enforcement', title: 'Enforcement in Ireland' },
  { id: 'assessment', title: 'How we assessed the site' },
  { id: 'date', title: 'Date of this statement' },
];

const mailto = `mailto:${site.email}?subject=Accessibility`;

const measures = [
  {
    title: 'Keyboard access.',
    body: 'Every link, button, menu, dialog and form field works from the keyboard, in a logical order. Dialogs hold focus while open, close with Escape and hand focus back to the control that opened them.',
  },
  { title: 'Skip link.', body: 'The first press of Tab on any page offers a link straight to the main content.' },
  {
    title: 'Visible focus.',
    body: 'A clear ring marks the element that has focus, on light, dark and footage backgrounds.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Contrast.',
    body: 'Text and controls meet the AA contrast ratios in both the light and the dark theme. Over footage, text sits on a tinted glass panel that holds the ratio whatever the film shows.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Reduced motion.',
    body: 'If your device asks for less motion, scroll reveals, drawn lines and the spinning sphere stay still, and each background film shows a still image until you press play.',
  },
  {
    title: 'A pause control on every film.',
    body: 'Each background film has a pause and play button. The films carry no audio and no information; they are decorative.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Text alternatives.',
    body: 'Images and diagrams that carry meaning have a text alternative. Decorative artwork is hidden from assistive technology.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Structure.',
    body: 'One main heading per page, headings in order without gaps, landmarks for the header, main content and footer, and the page language set to English (Ireland).',
  },
  {
    title: 'Forms.',
    body: 'Every field has a visible label. Errors appear as text beside the field, begin with the field name and are gathered in a summary. Colour alone never carries a message.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Target size.',
    body: 'Controls meet the WCAG 2.2 minimum target size, and the main buttons and menus offer 44 pixels or more.',
  },
  { title: 'Reflow.', body: 'Pages fold to a single column on narrow screens and under browser zoom.' },
  {
    title: 'Print.',
    body: 'A print stylesheet gives ink-on-white pages without footage or menus, with link addresses written out.',
  },
];
---

<Legal
  title="Accessibility statement: Viaclin"
  description="Viaclin aims to meet WCAG 2.2 level AA on viaclin.com. What we built in, the known limits, how to report a barrier and the enforcement route in Ireland."
  heading="Accessibility statement"
  lead="Our target is WCAG 2.2 level AA. This page sets out what we built in, where the limits are and how to tell us about a barrier."
  path="/accessibility"
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="commitment">Our commitment</h2>
  <p>
    Viaclin wants everyone to be able to read and use this site, whatever their device, ability or assistive
    technology. Our target is the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA, on every page and in
    both the light and the dark theme.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-we-did">What we did</h2>
  <ul>
    {measures.map((item) => <li><strong>{item.title}</strong> {item.body}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2 id="known-limits">Known limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Logos in the consultant experience banner.</strong> The third-party logos are images of text. WCAG treats
      logotypes as an exception, and each logo carries the company name as its text alternative. The banner has a pause
      button, pauses on hover and on focus, and becomes a static grid under reduced motion.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Background footage.</strong> The films are decorative. They have no audio, no captions and no audio
      description, because they hold no information that the page text does not give.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Site search.</strong> Search needs JavaScript. Without it, every page stays within reach through the
      header and footer links.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Wide tables.</strong> On a narrow screen the tables in the cookie policy and the privacy notice scroll
      sideways inside their own frame. The frame takes keyboard focus so that arrow keys can scroll it.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you find a limit that is not on this list, we want to hear about it.</p>

  <h2 id="report">Report a barrier</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={mailto}>{site.email}</a>. It helps if you tell us the address of the page, what you were trying to
    do, and the browser and assistive technology you use.
  </p>
  <p>
    We reply to every report. If you need the content of a page in another format, ask and we will send it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="enforcement">Enforcement in Ireland</h2>
  <p>
    If our answer does not settle the matter, the Equal Status Acts 2000 to 2018 prohibit discrimination in the
    provision of services, including on the ground of disability. Complaints under those Acts go to the
    {' '}<a href="https://www.workplacerelations.ie" rel="noopener noreferrer">Workplace Relations Commission</a>. The
    {' '}<a href="https://www.ihrec.ie" rel="noopener noreferrer">Irish Human Rights and Equality Commission</a> gives
    information on your rights.
  </p>

  <h2 id="assessment">How we assessed the site</h2>
  <p>
    Viaclin assessed the site itself. Every page runs through automated axe checks in both themes as part of the
    release process. We add manual checks with the keyboard alone, and we test at phone, tablet and desktop widths.
  </p>
  <p>Automated checks find some barriers and miss others, which is why your reports matter.</p>

  <h2 id="date">Date of this statement</h2>
  <p>
    This statement was prepared on {formatDate(site.legalUpdated)}. We review it when the site changes.
  </p>
</Legal>
